@shadowkon007 The statusline definitely supports ANSI escape codes.  I use them extensively in [ccstatusline](https://github.com/sirmalloc/ccstatusline) in 16 / 256 / truecolor modes and they output just fine in Terminal.app (16 / 256 only), iTerm2, ghostty, and VSCode.

I just updated my settings.json to this:

```
{
  "model": "opus",
  "statusLine": {
    "type": "command",
    "command": "printf \"\\033[33mHello\\033[0m\\n\"",
    "padding": 0
  }
}
```

